  "final_message": "The `OrderPlaced` event now carries `amountCents` and `createdAt`, but I did not remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. All 39 tests pass and `npm run arch` finds no violations.\n\n**Why I didn't do a plain rename:** billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event from other repos. Dropping the old names would break them as soon as this ships, and ARCH-4 says renames go through deprecation. So `totalCents` and `placedAt` stay on the event with the same values, marked `@deprecated`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** The `OrderPlaced` type has the new fields. `orderPlaced()` sets `createdAt` and `placedAt` to the order's placed time, and `amountCents` and `totalCents` to the order total.\n- **`schemaVersion`:** It stays at 3, since the change only adds fields.\n- **Tests:** I updated `test/app.test.ts` and `test/adapters.test.ts` to check both the new and the deprecated fields.\n- **Left alone:** The `GET /orders/{id}` response still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires it to stay backward compatible, and your request was about the event.\n\n**To finish the rename:** once both consumers read the new names, remove `totalCents` and `placedAt` from the event. That removal is a breaking change, so it probably needs a `schemaVersion` bump and coordination with those teams. I can prepare that change when you're ready.",
